Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:38:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rccl): optional UALoE fabric telemetry sampling (#12856)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## Motivation

optional UALoE fabric telemetry sampling

## Technical Details

Add RCCL_FABRIC_TELEMETRY_ENABLE, off by default, which samples every
amd-smi fabric telemetry category for the GPUs a process uses and logs
what moved every RCCL_FABRIC_TELEMETRY_INTERVAL_MS (default 1000,
floored at 100). It also needs RCCL_USE_AMD_SMI_LIB=1, since the sysfs
fabric path exposes no telemetry, and read access to the IFoE config
character device, which is root-only by default. Both are documented in
docs/api-reference/env-variables.rst. Anything missing disables
telemetry with a warning rather than failing init.

The counters are cumulative since firmware boot, so a sampler thread
diffs successive reads per device and reports the largest movers per
category, skipping datasets whose generation count has not advanced.
Releasing a device reports once more over its whole sampled lifetime,
because the firmware publishes only about once a second and a short run
can otherwise end with every tick having found the dataset stale.

Telemetry is keyed by GPU rather than by communicator and reference
counted. Each comm takes a reference on its own device in commAlloc and
drops it in commFree; a device's last comm frees its telemetry and the
last device stops the sampler. Sampling every GPU in the node instead
would have each rank of an n-GPU job do n times the work and emit n
duplicate log streams. Report lines carry the opening comm's hash,
matching the commId logged at Init START, and its rank, since the device
index alone does not identify the owning rank.

## Issue Tracking

JIRA ID : AICOMRCCL-571

## Test Plan

AmdSmiFabricTelemetryTests.cpp adds 25 tests over the sample reduction,
which is header-inline in amdsmi_wrap.h and needs no fabric hardware,
covering all 56 of its branches.

## Test Result

Unit tests: 25 added, all passing. AmdSmiFabricTelemetryTests.cpp is
registered in rccl-UnitTestsAmdSmi, which now runs 59 tests across 11
suites with no failures. The new tests split into five suites covering
category naming, interval clamping, the sample reduction, top-mover
selection, and fixed-size label handling. They exercise the reduction
through a fake telemetry sample that owns its datasets and instances, so
they need no fabric hardware and run in both Release and Debug.

Branch coverage: 56 of 56. All five extracted reduction functions report
100% region, line, and branch coverage; there are no uncovered branches
left to classify. The remaining uncovered functions in amdsmi_wrap.h are
the pre-existing fabric-layout helpers, which a separate suite covers.
The session plumbing — the sampler thread, refcounting, and the dlopen'd
amd-smi calls — is deliberately not unit-tested, since it needs a live
IFoE fabric; that side is covered by the hardware runs below.
